                <pb facs="es_d4-1" n="1" xml:id="es_d4-1"/>

                <head>ES–4. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>President Lemus of El Salvador made a
                    state visit to the United States, March 9–21, 1959. On March 11, he had
                    discussions with Acting Secretary of State Herter and President Eisenhower. Memoranda of these conversations are printed herein.
                    On the same day, Salvadoran Foreign Minister Ortíz Mancía and Economics Minister
                    Rochac met with Assistant Secretary of State Rubottom. A memorandum of this conversation is in decimal file
                    816.10/3–1159. Additional documentation on Lemus’ visit is in decimal file
                    716.11; and Conference Files, Lot 64 D 560, CF 1207 and 1207A. For further
                    information, see the Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>,
                    March 9, 1959, page 330; and <hi rendition="#italic">Public Papers of the
                        Presidents of the United States: Dwight D.
                            Eisenhower, 1959</hi>, pages 239, 241, and 253.</p>
            </div>
